.TH VCAMD 1 "2026-10-20" "vcam 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vcamd \- virtual camera daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vcamd
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-device
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR LEVEL ]
.RB [ \-\-write\-default\-config ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vcamd
holds a v4l2loopback device open and feeds it frames from a GStreamer
pipeline. Because the producer never stops, applications always see a normal
capture device. When nothing is playing the daemon writes a black placeholder.
.PP
The daemon does not need root. It should run as your user, with your account in
the
.B video
group, and it talks to clients over
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/vcam.sock .
.PP
A watchdog monitors the output pipeline. If frames stall, pushes keep failing,
or memory grows without bound, it rebuilds the pipeline. If repeated rebuilds do
not help it exits, so the systemd unit restarts it cleanly. The watchdog is
configured with the
.B [watchdog]
table; see
.IR ~/.config/vcam/config.toml .
.PP
The daemon detects which processes hold the camera open (same user only) and
defers any change that would renegotiate the device caps until they let go. With
.B auto_profiles
enabled it applies matching
.B [[profiles]]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config FILE
Configuration file. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/vcam/config.toml .
.TP
.B \-\-device PATH
Override the V4L2 device path, for example
.IR /dev/video10 .
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level LEVEL
One of
.IR error ,
.IR warn ,
.IR info ,
.IR debug " or " trace .
.TP
.B \-\-write\-default\-config
Write a default configuration file and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vcam/config.toml
Configuration file.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/vcamd.service
User service unit.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/modprobe.d/v4l2loopback.conf
Module options installed by the package.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vcam (1),
.BR vcam-gui (1),
.BR modprobe (8)
